# XGBoost Head Instead of MLP in Model_2

Replace the MLP regression head in the Informer+GAT pipeline with XGBoost. The neural backbone (Informer encoders → Gated Fusion → GAT) is trained end-to-end to learn spatial-temporal embeddings, then XGBoost does the final yield regression on those embeddings.

## Proposed Changes

### Model_2

#### [NEW] [train_xgboost_head.py](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/train_xgboost_head.py)

A new self-contained training script mirroring [train.py](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/train.py) but with a **two-stage pipeline**:

**Stage 1 — Backbone Training:**
- Train the full [DualChannelInformerGAT](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/informer_gat_model.py#284-438) model (with MLP head) using the same training loop as [train.py](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/train.py) (config, scaling, yield normalization, Huber loss, cosine scheduler)
- This is needed so the Informer encoders and GAT learn meaningful representations
- After training completes, restore best model checkpoint

**Stage 2 — XGBoost Head:**
- Freeze the backbone, run a forward pass on all data to extract post-GAT embeddings (`node_feat` from model output — shape `[S, N, D]` where D = `gat_hidden`)
- Flatten to `[S*N, D]` feature matrix with corresponding yield targets
- Split into train/val/test using the same season split as Stage 1
- Train an `XGBRegressor` on the train embeddings → yield
- Predict on all splits using XGBoost

**Analysis Outputs (same 7 artifacts as [train.py](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/train.py)):**
1. [metrics.json](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/analysis/run_6/metrics.json) — RMSE, MAE, MAPE, R² for all splits
2. [predictions.csv](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/analysis/run_6/predictions.csv) — Per-district actual vs predicted
3. [training_curves.png](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/analysis/run_6/training_curves.png) — Backbone train/val loss over epochs
4. [error_analysis.png](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/analysis/run_6/error_analysis.png) — Scatter + error histogram
5. [model_params.json](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/analysis/run_6/model_params.json) — Backbone params + XGBoost hyperparameters
6. `accuracy_classification.csv/png` — MAPE-based accuracy buckets
7. `trend_analysis.csv/png` — Year-over-year direction matching

**XGBoost Hyperparameters** (tunable via [config.yaml](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/Model_2/config.yaml) or defaults):
- `n_estimators=500`, `max_depth=6`, `learning_rate=0.05`
- `subsample=0.8`, `colsample_bytree=0.8`
- Early stopping on validation set (patience=50)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This requires `xgboost` to be installed. The existing [requirements.txt](file:///d:/IIT/Academics/BCS/wheat-yield-prediction/requirements.txt) does not list it, but `scikit-learn` is already there. We will add `xgboost` as an import dependency in the script.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
```bash
# Verify script compiles without errors
python -c "import py_compile; py_compile.compile('Model_2/train_xgboost_head.py', doraise=True)"

# Quick smoke test (3 epochs for backbone, then XGBoost)
python Model_2/train_xgboost_head.py --epochs 3
```

### Manual Verification
- Check that `Model_2/analysis/run_X/` is created with all 7 analysis artifact types
- Compare XGBoost head metrics against the MLP head metrics from previous runs
